  "text": {
    "intro": "The Mudflat Regatta is rowed over a course that is only a course at high tide, which is where most of the trouble starts.\nFive crews are involved. Determine each crew's placing, boat and colours.\n- **Crew**: the Almshouse crew, the Creamery crew, the Tannery crew, the Seminary crew and the Gasworks crew.\n- **Placing** (listed from better to worse): first, second, third, fourth and fifth.\n- **Boat**: the Peregrine, the Gilded Eel, the Obstinate, the Mudlark and the Last Resort.\n- **Colours**: bottle green; navy with a white band; cherry and grey; pink and cream; and lilac and bronze.\nEvery crew has a different placing, boat and colours, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
    "clues": [
      "The crew who rows the Obstinate and first are exactly three places apart in placing order.",
      "At least one of the following holds, and possibly more than one: (a) The Almshouse crew rows the Gilded Eel. (b) The Creamery crew and fourth both sit at odd-numbered places or both at even-numbered places.",
      "The following two do NOT both hold; either one alone may hold, and so may neither: (a) The Tannery crew does not finish fifth. (b) One of the crew who rows the Last Resort and the Creamery crew sits at an odd-numbered placing and the other at an even-numbered placing.",
      "The crew who wears pink and cream is exactly one place better than fifth, with no placing in between.",
      "The crew who rows the Peregrine and the Almshouse crew are exactly one place apart in placing order, in one direction or the other.",
      "The crew who wears bottle green is better than the Seminary crew in placing order.",
      "The crew who rows the Gilded Eel and the crew who wears cherry and grey are exactly one place apart in placing order, in one direction or the other.",
      "The crew who wears pink and cream is better than the crew who rows the Peregrine in placing order.",
      "The crew who rows the Last Resort and the crew who wears lilac and bronze are exactly four places apart in placing order.",
      "The crew who rows the Last Resort is exactly one place better than the crew who wears cherry and grey, with no placing in between."
    ]
  }
